WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.600
Let's take a quick look at how to create and
use Service Accounts. Service Accounts are

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.650
used when you want to authenticate machines,
such as Compute Engine VMs, to use other Google

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:13.240
Cloud Services. To create a Service Account,
go to the Permissions page. Go to the "Service

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.830
Accounts" tab, and click "Create service account."
Give your new Service Account a name, and

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:23.010
make sure you furnish a new private key. Keep
this key safe, as you cannot download it again.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.910
Let's go to the "Permissions" tab to lock
down this Service Account. Search for your

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.090
Service Account, and then click Role(s). I
only want this Service Account to create Disks

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.399
and Snapshots, so I'm gonna remove the "Editor"
role and add the "Compute Storage Admin" role

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:40.269
instead. In my Compute Engine instance, I've
already copied my private key over. In this

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:44.269
example, I'm going to use the gcloud to create
a snapshot. Use the Service Account email

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:49.319
and key file with the "activate-service-account"
command. Now use "gcloud init" to configure

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:53.569
gcloud to use our new Service Account. This
Service Account only has Compute Storage Admin

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:58.109
scope. If we try to create a new instance,
it will fail, but if we try to create a new

00:00:58.109 --> 00:00:59.409
disk, it will work fine!

